.TH SHEDMAN-DOCTOR 1 "2026-04-25" "ShedOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shedman-doctor \- read-only drift detector for /etc/shedos/system.toml
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shedman doctor
.RB [ -c | --config
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B shedman doctor
.RB [ -j | --json ]
|
.RB [ -d | --diff ]
|
.RB [ -f | --fix ]
|
.B --waybar
|
.B --tick
|
.B --notify-if-new
|
.B --reset-notify-state
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shedman doctor
runs the same plan engine as
.BR shedman-apply (1)
but never mutates anything. It returns a Plan describing the
differences between
.I /etc/shedos/system.toml
and the live system. Outputs vary by mode:
.TP
default (no flag)
Print a compact, colorized summary of every drift item.
.TP
.BR -j , " --json"
Emit a machine-readable JSON document suitable for the
.B custom/doctor
waybar module. Includes a stable
.I plan_hash
fingerprint.
.TP
.BR -d , " --diff"
Render unified diffs for every drift entry. Useful before running
.BR "shedman apply" .
.TP
.BR -f , " --fix"
Delegate to
.BR "shedman apply --yes"
and exit with whatever code apply returns. Safe shorthand for
\(oqI looked at the diff, just do it\(cq.
.TP
.B --waybar
JSON shape consumed by waybar's
.B custom/doctor
module. Always exits 0 even on drift.
.TP
.B --tick
Timer-driven entrypoint. Notify-if-new + refresh waybar; always
exits 0.
.TP
.B --notify-if-new
Fire a mako notification iff the drift fingerprint has changed
since the last invocation.
.TP
.B --reset-notify-state
Clear the hysteresis file. Use this if a notification got stuck.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/shedos/system.toml
Source of truth (read-only).
.TP
.I /var/lib/shedos/doctor.state.json
Hysteresis file (last-notified plan_hash).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Same overrides as
.BR shedman-apply (1):
SHEDOS_APPLY_ETC_ROOT, _STATE_ROOT, _SYSTEMCTL, _UFW, _PACMAN_KEY,
_FSTAB_PATH, _BOOT_ROOT.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Aligned, or drift found (default mode + waybar/tick modes).
.TP
.B 1
.B --fix
delegated to apply, which returned non-zero.
.TP
.B 2
Schema or environment-shape error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shedman (1),
.BR shedman-apply (1).
